    "text": "# Investigation note: metric M343112, reporting month 2026-10-31\n\n## 1. Executive finding\nM343112's provisional rate is **63.0% (17 of 27)**, which puts it in the provisional **Red** band (needs attention). That is up **18.1 percentage points** from 44.8% (13 of 29) at 2026-09-30, a move from Green to Red in one month. Two things drove the change: the 19 applications reported in both months scored higher, and the mix of reporting applications changed. There is also a definitional conflict to resolve before this result is acted on (see section 7).\n\n## 2. Current status and period (2026-10-31)\n- 27 metric rows from 27 applications. Every row is in the denominator, which fits the INCLUDES_PENDING denominator scope.\n- Compliance status of the rows: 17 Compliant, 6 Non_Compliant, 4 Pending, 0 Not_Applicable.\n- Over the 12 month-ends from 2025-11-30 the provisional rate ranged from 36.0% to 64.0%. October's 63.0% is the third-highest month, just below December 2025 and June 2026 (both 64.0%).\n## 3. Movement against 2026-09-30 (provisional)\nThese are observed counts. They show who reported, not why the rate moved.\n- **Applications in both months (19):** rate rose from 8 of 19 (42.1%) to 11 of 19 (57.9%).\n- **Only in October (8):** 6 of 8 in the numerator (75.0%), which pushes the rate up.\n- **Only in September (12):** 5 of 10 in the numerator (50.0%) before they dropped out.\n- **Status changes among the 19 continuing applications:** 2 newly non-compliant, 5 resolved, 2 non-compliant in both months.\n- **Non-compliant rows** fell from 10 (of 31) to 6 (of 27).\n\n## 4. Main contributors (October's 6 non-compliant rows)\n| Super division | Rows | Legal entity | Applications |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Super_Division_04 | 2 | Legal_Entity_38 (both) | Application_00221, Application_01246 |\n| Super_Division_06 | 2 | Legal_Entity_39 (both) | Application_01080, Application_00922 |\n| Super_Division_02 | 1 | Legal_Entity_31 | Application_01083 |\n| Super_Division_03 | 1 | Legal_Entity_13 | Application_01155 |\n\nSuper_Division_05, 07 and 08 have no non-compliant rows. With only 1 or 2 rows per group, these concentrations are too small to treat as patterns.\n## 5. Testing and exceptions\n- **Failed tests:** 8 completed tests failed, the same as September and the joint highest in the 12-month series.\n  - 5 of the 8 are non-compliant: 3 Test_Failed, 1 Open_Findings_Outstanding, 1 Remediation_Overdue.\n  - 2 are recorded as Compliant despite the failed test: one Compensating_Control_Accepted, one Remediation_Verified.\n  - 1 is Pending (Remediation_In_Progress).\n- **Other non-compliant row:** 1 with No_Test_Performed.\n- **Pending rows (4):** 2 Awaiting_Test_Assignment, 1 Test_In_Progress, 1 Remediation_In_Progress. All 4 count in the denominator.\n- **Exemptions:** 1 row is Exempt and recorded as Compliant (Exemption_Conditions_Met).\n\n## 6. Areas to investigate further (hypotheses, not findings)\n- Why 8 applications entered and 12 left the metric's population in one month. That turnover accounts for part of the 18.1 pp rise.\n- Whether the two failed tests recorded as Compliant should count in the numerator.\n- Whether the paired rows under Legal_Entity_38 and Legal_Entity_39 share a common factor. Nothing in the data shows one yet.\n- How long the 4 Pending rows stay unresolved, since they sit in the denominator.\n\n## 7. Limitations of the evidence\n- **The meaning of the rate is unclear.** In this data, all 17 numerator rows are Compliant and no Non_Compliant row is in the numerator. So the October rise coincides with more Compliant rows and fewer non-compliant ones. That conflicts with the supplied rule that a higher rate is worse. I have kept the supplied Red band, but its direction and the numerator's business meaning need client confirmation before anyone acts on it.\n- The rate, the band thresholds (45% and 60%) and the movement categories are all provisional. None of them is a client target.\n- The denominator scope (INCLUDES_PENDING) is inferred from Pending rows only.\n- The population is small (27 rows), so a single row moves the rate by about 3.7 pp.\n- No metric name, metric family or cause data is available. Nothing in this note identifies owners or confirms that remediation is complete.\n- All names are synthetic.\nI've reached the time limit for this request. The analysis may be incomplete.\n\nWould you like me to continue working on this?",
